Deferred. Do not start this without the trigger below.

Project fields are single-line key: value, so they cannot hold a set, and
there is no equivalent of bd's label filtering. A comma-separated field
covers the simple case badly: it invites parsing inside a value, which is
the thing the format has otherwise avoided everywhere.

Trigger: wanting to filter across a dimension that is not already a field.
Until then, adding a field is cheaper and reads better.

28 changes the calculation slightly — once values are validated by a
pattern, a comma-separated set has a grammar that check could enforce
rather than a convention it cannot see. That makes the bad option less bad,
not good.


Evidence from 38, 2026-09-18. ../idol used beads for sixteen months and its
labels amount to one distinct value — feedback-2026-07-22, a dated batch
marker on 33 issues from a single afternoon's triage. No taxonomy ever
formed, and nothing was ever filtered across one. The trigger stands and has
not fired. Keep deferred.
